    <h2>What makes Level 28 tricky<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The ghost absorbs six of the sixteen moves: the towel at 1, the nurse's coat at 2, the bandage at 4, the notebook and pen at 5, the hammer at 8 and the pump at 11 all end on the same patient. That builds a habit — find an object, drag it to the ghost — which the level breaks at steps 6, 7 and 9. The candy goes to the child at step 6, the cosmetics to the girl at step 7, the scissors to the boy at step 9. Four patients share one waiting room, and the ghost is only the largest of them.</p>
    <p>Two cards carry more than one thing. Step 5 is the notebook and the pen together, so a single drag has two objects in it, and step 12 is a click on the photo in the ghost's hand rather than on the ghost. The target there is the size of a card, not the size of a figure. Step 3 is the only swipe: the axe hangs above the ghost's head and has to be pushed up out of the way. Fourteen of the sixteen moves are drags, one is that click, one is that swipe, which makes the odd gesture the easiest thing in the clinic to get wrong.</p>
    <p>The last four cards change cast. Step 13 sends the sleeping ghost's clothes to the doctor, step 14 sends the scissors to the sleeping ghost, step 15 sends the cut hair to the doctor, and step 16 drags the doctor to the ghost bride. That is a haircut and a costume change performed on a second ghost, and the recipient of both is the doctor, not the sleeping ghost whose clothes and hair they are. The scissors, already handed to the boy at step 9, come back out at 14; a run that treated them as spent stops one card short. The final drag is also the only person-to-person move in the level.</p>

    <h2>Four patients, one clinic<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
    <p>The ghost takes six items, but three of the middle cards belong to somebody else:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>The ghost collects the towel, the nurse's coat, the bandage, the notebook and pen, the hammer and the pump (steps 1, 2, 4, 5, 8, 11).</li>
      <li>The candy, the cosmetics and the scissors go to the child, the girl and the boy instead (steps 6, 7, 9).</li>
      <li>Step 5 is two objects in one drag: the notebook and the pen.</li>
      <li>The axe above the ghost's head is a swipe up, the only swipe in the sixteen moves.</li>
      <li>The photo in the ghost's hand is a click, and the target is the photo rather than the ghost.</li>
      <li>The scissors come back out at step 14, this time on the sleeping ghost.</li>
      <li>The sleeping ghost's clothes and the cut hair both go to the doctor, and the doctor goes to the ghost bride.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Count the patients before you count the props: four of them are being treated and only one stands in the middle of the room.</p>

    <h2>FAQ<span class="accent">.</span></h2>
   
    <details><summary>What is the answer to Brain Puzzle 3 Level 28?</summary><p>In order: 1) Drag the towel to the ghost; 2) Drag the nurse's coat to the ghost; 3) Swipe up the axe above the ghost's head; 4) Drag the bandage to the ghost; 5) Drag the notebook and pen to the ghost; 6) Drag the candy to the child; 7) Drag the cosmetics to the girl; 8) Drag the hammer to the ghost; 9) Drag the scissors to the boy; 10) Drag Cupid's bow and arrow to the boy; 11) Drag the pump to the ghost; 12) Click the photo in the ghost's hand; 13) Drag the sleeping ghost's clothes to the doctor; 14) Drag the scissors to the sleeping ghost; 15) Drag the cut hair to the doctor; 16) Drag the doctor to the ghost bride</p></details>
    <details><summary>Why does nothing happen when I tap in Level 28?</summary><p>Drags are almost the whole level: the axe above the ghost's head wants a swipe up at step 3, and the photo in the ghost's hand wants a click at step 12, which is the only tap in the clinic.</p></details>
